---
title: Chinese Tomato Egg Stir Fry
servings: 2
cuisine: Chinese
tags: stir-fry, vegetarian, egg, rice
image: https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/rwvw8q1765660071.jpg
source: https://www.simplyrecipes.com/chinese-tomato-egg-recipe-7562056
---

Slice the @tomato{450%g} in half. Remove the tough stem from each half that connects to the vine. Cut each half into equal thirds (you’ll get 6 slices from each tomato).

In a cold, 8 to 10-inch nonstick #frying pan{}, add the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} and @egg{5}(beaten). Turn the heat to medium. Once a thin layer of eggs is just beginning to cook on the bottom, push the eggs in one direction to create layers of scrambled eggs.

Cook, gently stirring the whole time, until the scrambled eggs are mostly set but still slightly wet and shiny, ~{3%minutes}. Remove the eggs to a #plate{} and, if needed, wipe out the pan.

Add the @sesame oil{1%tsp} to the #frying pan{} followed by the tomatoes and stir-fry over medium heat until the tomatoes are softened but not mushy, about ~{3%minutes}. Add the @chicken bouillon powder{2%tsp}, @sugar{2%tsp}, and @black pepper{0.5%tsp}. Toss until combined and the sugar and bouillon have dissolved, about ~{1%minute}.

Add the eggs back to the pan with the tomatoes. Stir-fry for about ~{2%minutes} to heat through and combine. Taste, adding @?salt{0.25%tsp} only if needed. Sprinkle with the @spring onion{1} and serve with steamed @jasmine rice{400%g}.
